---
import Slide from '../ui/Slide.astro';
import Matrix from '../ui/Matrix.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '../ui/Callout.astro';
---

<Slide
  id="s39b-net-service-commands"
  chapter="Failure Patterns"
  title="Service — Diagnose Fast"
  notes="The 10-second check: get svc, get endpoints, get pods --show-labels. Selector mismatch: compare svc jsonpath selector to pod labels. From client pod: curl http://svc.ns.svc:port. Works by IP not DNS → DNS issue. ExternalName returns CNAME — curl external directly. EndpointSlice mirroring for external backends — mention briefly."
>
  <div class="stagger flex flex-col gap-8">
    <Matrix
      headers={['Symptom', 'Check', 'Common fix']}
      rows={[
        ['Endpoints &lt;none&gt;', 'svc selector vs pod labels', 'Align labels'],
        ['Refused on correct IP', 'targetPort ≠ containerPort', 'Fix Service targetPort'],
        ['Works by IP not DNS', 'Resolution path', 'nslookup svc.ns.svc'],
        ['Stale IPs briefly', 'Terminated pods in slice', 'Wait or check readiness flapping'],
      ]}
    />

    <CodeBlock
      caption="Service → Pod path"
      code={`kubectl get svc SVC -n NAMESPACE -o wide
kubectl get endpoints SVC -n NAMESPACE -o wide
kubectl get pods -n NAMESPACE --show-labels

kubectl exec CLIENT -n NAMESPACE -- \\
  curl -sv http://SVC.NAMESPACE.svc.cluster.local:PORT/health`}
    />

    <Callout type="myth" title="Myth">
      "Service is broken because kubectl get svc shows CLUSTER-IP." — Svc is virtual; endpoints are real.
    </Callout>
  </div>
</Slide>
